         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/eac061c9-fd82-4c61-a33c-4171ac6da743,1794865319829/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%2820%2C0%2C1139%2C640%29%3B' alt='Toronto Maple Leafs head coach Jim Hiller looks on past Gavin McKenna during a September 19, 2026 NHL pre-season game against the visiting Montreal Canadiens.' width='620' height='349' title='Maple Leafs GM John Chayka says he has &apos;a lot of confidence&apos; in first-year bench boss Jim Hiller and his staff despite an 8-12-2 record that puts Toronto last in the Atlantic Division, already nine points out of a playoff spot.'/><p>Toronto Maple Leafs general manager John Chayka backed head coach Jim Hiller while speaking to reporters at Monday's practice. The team has lost eight of its last nine games in regulation, including six straight on a disastrous recent homestand.</p>]]></description>
